declare cid uuid;
begin
  select id into cid from public.courses where slug = 'bib-102';
  insert into public.course_items (course_id, kind, position, title, content) select cid, 'topic', 13, $j$4.1 Ephesians: Grace, Unity and the Armor of God$j$, $j${"readings": [{"title": "Ephesians 2 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Ephesians/2"}, {"title": "Ephesians 4 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Ephesians/4"}, {"title": "Ephesians 6 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Ephesians/6"}], "body": "Read Ephesians 2, Ephesians 4 and Ephesians 6 in the King James Version. Then read this lesson.\n\nEphesus was one of the great cities of Asia Minor, and Paul had spent about three years there teaching the Word. He wrote the letter to the Ephesians while he was in prison. Ephesians is a letter about the church. In chapter 2 Paul wrote that we are saved by grace through faith, and that salvation is the gift of God and not of works. In chapter 4 he urged believers to keep the unity of the Spirit in the bond of peace and to be kind and forgiving to one another. In chapter 6 he taught that believers face a spiritual battle and must put on the whole armor of God to stand against the devil.\n\nKey words: grace, workmanship, unity, armor, sword of the Spirit.\n\nYour task: (1) Write Ephesians 2:8 and 9 in your own words. (2) Tell why Paul urged believers to keep unity in Ephesians 4. (3) Name at least four pieces of the armor of God and tell what the sword of the Spirit is.\n\nCourse area: Bible elective. Scripture is read from the King James Version.", "video": "", "presenter": "Dr. Alex L. Jenkins Sr.", "standards": "Bible elective", "script": "Welcome to Unit 4. We continue with the letters of Paul. Four of them, Ephesians, Philippians, Colossians and Philemon, were written while Paul was in prison, so they are often called the prison letters. Paul was chained, but the Word of God was not chained, and these letters have encouraged believers for almost two thousand years.\n\nEphesus was a major city of Asia Minor, famous for its great temple of the goddess Diana. Paul spent about three years there on his third journey, and a strong church was planted. Later he wrote this letter to help the believers understand who they are in Christ and how the church is to live.\n\nIn chapter 2 Paul gave one of the clearest statements of salvation in the Bible. Ephesians 2:8 says, For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God: Verse 9 adds, Not of works, lest any man should boast. We cannot save ourselves. Then verse 10 tells us what we are saved for. For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works, which God hath before ordained that we should walk in them. We are saved by grace, and then we are given good works to do.\n\nIn chapter 4 Paul turned to the life of the church. Ephesians 4:3 says, Endeavouring to keep the unity of the Spirit in the bond of peace. The church is not a building. It is one body. Verse 4 says, There is one body, and one Spirit, even as ye are called in one hope of your calling; And verse 32 gives a daily command, And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God for Christ's sake hath forgiven you. Unity grows when we forgive.\n\nChapter 6 teaches that the Christian life includes a spiritual battle. Ephesians 6:10 says, Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might. Verse 11 says, Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil. Verse 12 explains, For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places. Paul then listed the armor: the girdle of truth, the breastplate of righteousness, feet shod with the preparation of the gospel of peace, the shield of faith, the helmet of salvation and the sword of the Spirit. Verse 17 says, And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God: The sword is the one piece of armor that is used to attack, and it is the Word of God.\n\nYour task is to write Ephesians 2:8 and 9 in your own words, tell why Paul urged believers to keep unity, and name at least four pieces of the armor of God. Then take the four question check.\n\nWe are saved by grace, we are kept by unity, and we stand by the Word. Excellence, Faith, Purpose. I will see you in the next lesson."}$j$::jsonb where not exists (select 1 from public.course_items where course_id = cid and kind = 'topic' and title = $j$4.1 Ephesians: Grace, Unity and the Armor of God$j$);
end
$seed$;
